  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Limited edition of 120 copies.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"To celebrate Hildegard's nine hundredth birthday. Claire Van Vliet made the pulp paintings with Katie MacGregor in Whiting, Me., who also made the colored sheets and covers ... the popups were executed by Audrey Holden, the chemise &amp; slipcase by Judi Conant &amp; Mary Richardson in Maidstone, Vermont ... The cover lettering is Circulus Sapientiae in Hildegard's secret alphabet"--Colophon in booklet.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Accordion-fold format with seven pop-up illustrations.  In a cloth covered portfolio with the booklet and music CD in a paper pocket, in a slipcase.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
